WEBVTT

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.160
-Wait, what? What happened?
-(CLATTERING)

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.600
-(FEAR AND JOY GASP)
-A Core Memory!

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.720
Oh, no!

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.960
Sadness, what are you doing?

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.080
SADNESS: It looked like
one was crooked

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.080
so I opened it and then it fell out.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.160
I...

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.400
Whoo-hoo!

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.840
It's just that...
I wanted to maybe hold one.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.320
-FEAR: Joy!
-Whoa, whoa!

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.720
Sadness, you nearly
touched a Core Memory.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.120
And when you touch them,
we can't change them back.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.360
I know. I'm sorry.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.240
Something's wrong with me.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.200
It's like I'm having a breakdown.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.360
You're not having
a breakdown. It's stress.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.120
I keep making mistakes like that.
I'm awful.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.360
-No, you're not.
-And annoying.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.440
(STUTTERING) You know what?

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.440
You can't focus on what's going wrong.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.200
There's always a way to
turn things around,

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.720
to find the fun.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.640
Yeah. Find the fun.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.440
I don't know how to do that.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.840
Okay. Well,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.400
try to think of something funny.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.800
Um... Oh!

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.600
Remember the funny movie
where the dog dies?

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.640
Oh. Yeah, that's not...

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:10.400
What about that time with Meg

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.400
when Riley laughed so hard

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.520
milk came out of her nose?

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.840
(LAUGHING)

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.400
Yeah. That hurt. It felt like fire.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.080
SADNESS: Ooh, it was awful.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:22.880
Okay, okay, don't think of that.
Let's try something else.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.640
Uh, what are your favorite things to do?

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:25.960
My favorite?

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.440
Um... Well, I like it when we're outside.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.440
That's good. Like there's
the beach and sunshine.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:32.880
Oh! Like that time

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.680
we buried Dad
in the sand up to his neck.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.000
SADNESS: I was thinking more like rain.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.600
Rain? Rain is my favorite, too!

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:43.520
We can stomp around in puddles.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:46.800
JOY: You know, there's cool umbrellas,
lightning storms.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:48.880
SADNESS: More like when
the rain runs down our back

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.480
and makes our shoes soggy.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.840
And we get all cold, shivery, and

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.720
everything just starts
feeling droopy. (CRYING)

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.960
Oh, hey, hey. Hey, easy.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:00.560
Why are you crying?

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.120
It's just like really the opposite
of what we're going for here.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.800
Crying helps me slow down and obsess

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.040
over the weight of life's problems.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.240
(JOY SIGHS)

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:11.680
You know what? Let's, uh,

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.080
think about something else. (GRUNTS)

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.960
How about we read
some mind manuals, huh?

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.200
-Sounds fun.
-I've read most of them.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.080
Well, have you read this one?
This seems interesting.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.360
"Long Term Memory Retrieval,
Volume 47"?

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.720
-No.
-Ooh, a real page-turner!

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.920
"Long Term Memory data selection

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.640
"via channel subgrouping"?

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:32.240
See? Fun already! Oh, you lucky dog.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:33.640
You're reading these cool things.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.960
I got to go work. Life is so unfair.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.320
(SIGHS)

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.080
(BELL DINGS)

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:43.960
(GROANS)

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.000
DAD: What can we do?
We've only got capital

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.560
to last a month, maybe two.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:50.600
If we can't find investors by then,

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.040
we're going to have to lay people off.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.320
Mom! Dad!

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.760
Come kiss me good night!

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.200
DAD: I know. I know.
MOM: Be right there!

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.000
DAD: We've got to land this, okay?

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.840
Did you hear Dad?
He sounded really upset.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.360
-(VEHICLE PASSING)
-(GASPS)

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:06.760
(RUMBLING)

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.080
What was that?
Was it a bear? It's a bear!

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.680
There are no bears in San Francisco.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.800
I saw a really hairy guy.
He looked like a bear.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.200
Oh, I'm so jumpy. My nerves are shot.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.600
Ew! I don't want to
hear about your nerves.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.480
I'll tell you what it is.
This move has been a bust.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.080
FEAR: That's what I've been
telling you guys!

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.560
There are at least 37 things for
Riley to be scared of right now.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.280
The smell alone is
enough to make her gag.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.280
ANGER: I can't believe
Mom and Dad moved us here!

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.640
Look, I get it. You guys have concerns.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.040
But we've been through worse!

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:32.960
Tell you what,
let's make a list of all the things

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.760
Riley should be happy about.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.760
Fine. Let's see, this house stinks,
our room stinks.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.760
-Pizza is weird here.
-Our friends are back home.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.600
And all of our stuff is in the missing van!

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.320
Oh, come on. It could be worse.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:46.320
Yeah, Joy. We could be
lying on the dirty floor. In a bag.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.000
Okay, I admit it, we had a rough start.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.600
But think of all the good things that...

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.000
No, Joy. There's
absolutely no reason for Riley

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.320
to be happy right now.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:55.560
Let us handle this.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:56.800
I say we skip school tomorrow

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.080
and lock ourselves in the bedroom.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.840
We have no clean clothes.
I mean, no one should see us.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.560
Yeah, we could cry
until we can't breathe.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.360
We should lock the door
and scream that curse word we know.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.120
-It's a good one!
-Now hold on!

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.240
Look, we all have our off days.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.400
-You know...
-Hi, honey.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.160
The Mom bad news train is pulling in.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:14.320
Toot-toot!

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:16.320
Still no moving van. (SCOFFS)

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.120
Now they're saying it won't be here
till Tuesday, can you believe it?

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.240
Toot-toot-toot!

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.120
-Where's Dad?
-On the phone.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.560
This new venture
is keeping him pretty busy.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:26.120
I rest my case!

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.840
MOM: Oh, your dad's a little stressed,

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.960
you know, about getting
his new company up and running.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.520
Now for a few
well-placed withering scowls.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.080
(SIGHS)

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.400
I guess all I really
want to say is, thank you.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.000
-Huh?
-MOM: You know,

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:42.080
through all this confusion
you've stayed...

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.320
(LAUGHS) Well,
you've stayed our happy girl.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.080
MOM: Your dad's
under a lot of pressure,

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.080
but if you and I can keep smiling,

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.440
it would be a big help.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.120
We can do that for him. Right?

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.400
Whoa.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.560
JOY: Well.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:01.280
Yeah, sure.

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:03.600
What did we do to deserve you?

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.320
-Sweet dreams.
-RILEY: Good night.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:12.880
Well, you can't argue with Mom.
Happy it is.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.320
Team Happy! Sounds great!

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.480
Totally behind you, Joy.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.880
Looks like we're going into REM.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.400
I got Dream Duty, so I'll take care

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.880
of sending these to Long Term.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.600
JOY: Great day today, guys!

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:25.640
-Oh, sleep well, Team Happy!
-(ALL TALKING AT ONCE)

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.520
All right,
what's on tonight, Dream Production?

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:31.400
(MUSIC PLAYING)

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.360
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.200
Well, this is it. The new place.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:38.960
(THUNDER CRASHING)

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.160
(VOICES MOANING)

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:43.120
Come live with me, Riley. (GRUNTS)

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.600
Somebody order a broccoli pizza?

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.120
-Eat me!
-I'm organic!

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.960
(SIGHS) No! Who is in charge
of programming down there?

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.160
I know I'm not supposed to do this, but...

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.360
We are not going to
end the day like this.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.280
(RILEY LAUGHING)

